 to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535167 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535187 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535167 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535167 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $b\\cdot ((-4)c\\times 3a)$, if $4a\\cdot (2b\\times (-4)c)=-128.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535167 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "371a5e09-afe1-5a22-8d4f-574703d014c6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535167 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (2b\\times (-4)c) & =-128 \\\\ 4\\cdot 2\\cdot (-4)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =-128 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring out the constants in the requested product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot ((-4)c\\times 3a) & =(-4)\\cdot 3[b\\cdot (c\\times a)] \\\\ & =(-4)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4 \\\\ & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535186 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535180 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535186 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535186 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $b\\cdot (a\\times c)$, if $(-7)a\\cdot (b\\times c)=-28.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535186 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6d5dd27d-8ce5-5b7e-9ce7-851473477c43" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186535186 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7)a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-28 \\\\ (-7)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =-28 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$